  "asr_text": "Meanwhile, U.S. consumer price data showed that the price of coffee was 6.1% higher than in the same month a year earlier. It may leave you wondering, did prices go down or up? But the data covers a different month from the bean price measure, and it does not show the price of a cup at a cafe. Hold on before putting the two figures in the ring. So how long does it take for the price of beans to reach a price tag? According to estimates from market insiders and experts interviewed by Reuters, it takes at least about nine months for the price of raw beans to show up in U.S. retail prices. The road to a price tag is quite a long journey. The article says that companies in the U.S. that roast coffee keep raw beans in stock. Roasting and packing the beans also take time. They also often negotiate prices with retailers on a regular basis. The price tag in a shop does not flash to a new price the moment the market moves.",
